  "uses_raw": true,
  "prompt": "Marieke, the CFO, asks which orders were rung up with prices in cents, so that finance can restate each receipt. These tables may hold errors. A line is priced in cents when its unit_price_eur is more than 10 times its product's unit_cost_eur; its unit price in euros is then unit_price_eur divided by 100, while line_discount_eur is in euros already. A line's revenue is quantity times its unit price minus line_discount_eur. Return one row for each order with at least one line priced in cents, in any store and any month, with five columns in this order: order_id; store_code; n_lines, the order's lines priced in cents; revenue_stored_eur, the revenue of those lines as stored; and revenue_fixed_eur, the revenue of those lines with the unit price in euros. Do not round. Sort by order_id from low to high.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "order_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "store_code",
        "type_class": "text"
      },
      {
        "name": "n_lines",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
